 other low-lying and flood-prone location.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Runoff from heavy rain and melting snow over the San Juan\nMountains may cause flooding in the San Luis Valley, especially\nMonday and Tuesday as high flows move out of the mountains and\nthrough the Rio Grande and Conejos River.\n- The greatest risk of flooding will be along the Conejos River and\nthe Rio Grande, including Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood http://cotrip.org","ends":"2026-11-04T05:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Del Norte Vicinity/Northern San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Alamosa  Vicinity/Central San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Southern San Luis Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a6499198bfeb3e5888538271cdeb42f7320e5f04.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a6499198bfeb3e5888538271cdeb42f7320e5f04.002.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 1 at 7:26PM MST until November 2 at 7:30PM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"Upstream flooding along the Rio Grande continues downstream near\nMonte Vista in Rio Grande County.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding along the Rio Grande near Monte Vista is forecasted\nto begin by late morning on Monday.\n\n* WHERE...East Central Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 730 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...The Rio Grande continues to rise due to upstream flooding\nthrough Del Norte and South Fork. Extensive inundation of low-lying\nareas adjacent to the river is expected. Inundation of low spots\nalong Highway 185, some homes, and other structures may be possible\nfor areas south of the river. Expect many areas of slow moving or\nstanding water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 717 PM MST, Upstream stream gauges on the Rio Grande and South\nFork Rio Grande indicate that flooding is occurring.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMonte Vista.\n- 